<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal-Basis mostly flat, movement slow.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal-Basis mostly flat, movement slow.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. rail and truck soymeal basis offers were mostly steady on Friday with very little activity noted as end-users continued to wait for the CBOT September contract to expire, several brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Things will start getting interesting next week as everybody makes the transition over to the Oct from the September,&quot; an Ohio broker said. &quot;(Sellers) are holding onto the September as long as they can.&quot;</p>
<p>The September contract was trading at a $9.80 per ton premium to the October. Harvest pressure was expected to push October prices even lower, traders said.</p>
<p>The September contract expires on Thursday next week.</p>
<p>Bids slipped $1.00 per ton in Kansas City and Fostoria, Ohio but firmed $1.00 in Lancaster, Penn.  </p>
